{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VnXvHHz4PazwFyUT3v7mgi","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's your comprehensive guide to the patterns used in this Go Unix utilities codebase:\n\n## 1. Simple cmd/ Utility Structure: cmd/cut/main.go\n\nThe `cut` utility demonstrates a clean, straightforward pattern:\n\n**Key structural elements:**\n- **SIGPIPE handler**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start of main (handles broken pipe gracefully)\n- **Buffered I/O**: Uses `bufio.Writer` for stdout to batch writes efficiently\n- **Error handling**: Errors go to stderr with the command name prefix (e.g., `\"cut: %s\\n\"`)\n- **Exit codes**: Uses `os.Exit(exitCode)` after cleanup\n- **Flag parsing**: Custom parser (not flags package) handling both short (`-f`) and long (`--output-delimiter`) forms\n- **File processing**: Supports stdin, explicit stdin via `-`, and multiple file arguments\n- **Validation**: Validates options before processing (mutual exclusivity checks)\n\nThe main flow: `parseArgs()` → `processFiles()` → specific processing functions → `w.Flush()` → `os.Exit()`.\n\n**File location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5449/cmd/cut/main.go` (427 lines)\n\n---\n\n## 2. cmd/ Test File Pattern: cmd/cut/cut_test.go\n\nTests use a differential testing approach:\n\n```go\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcut\")  // GNU reference binary\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n    }\n    \n    // Setup test fixtures\n    dir := t.TempDir()\n    writeFile(t, dir, \"fields.txt\", \"a:b:c\\n\")\n    \n    // Define normalizers for output comparison\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        {\n            Name:  \"r4_1_exit_zero_field_stdin\",\n            Args:  []string{\"-d:\", \"-f2\"},\n            Stdin: []byte(\"a:b:c\\n\"),\n        },\n        // ... more tests\n    }\n    \n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- Builds the Go binary being tested\n- Looks up GNU reference binary (gsplit, gcut, etc.)\n- Skips tests if reference not available\n- Uses DiffTest structs with `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `WorkDir`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize`\n- `ExpectedFiles` field for testing file-producing commands\n- Normalizers transform output before comparison (regex replacements, lowercasing, etc.)\n\n**File location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5449/cmd/cut/cut_test.go` (102 lines)\n\n---\n\n## 3. DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nFrom `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5449/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 30-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string           // Subtest name (used with t.Run)\n    Args          []string         // Command-line args for both binaries\n    Stdin         []byte           // nil = EOF, []byte{} = open then closed\n    Env           []string         // KEY=VALUE pairs merged with process env\n    WorkDir       string           // Working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n    ExitCode      int              // Expected exit code (default 0)\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc   // Output transformations before comparison\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte // For file-producing commands\n}\n```\n\n**ExpectedFiles usage** (lines 211-227):\n```go\nfunc checkExpectedFiles(t *testing.T, workDir string, expected map[string][]byte) {\n    t.Helper()\n    if expected == nil {\n        return\n    }\n    for relPath, want := range expected {\n        fullPath := filepath.Join(workDir, relPath)\n        got, err := os.ReadFile(fullPath)\n        if err != nil {\n            t.Fatalf(\"expected file %s: %v\", relPath, err)\n        }\n        if !bytes.Equal(got, want) {\n            t.Fatalf(\"file %s divergence\\n  expected: %q\\n  actual:   %q\",\n                relPath, want, got)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nMaps relative paths to expected byte content. After both binaries run in the same working directory, each file listed is checked for exact byte-for-byte match.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Example with ExpectedFiles: cmd/split/split_test.go\n\nShows how file-producing commands are tested:\n\n```go\nfunc lineSplitTests() []testutils.DiffTest {\n    return []testutils.DiffTest{\n        {\n            Name:  \"default_1000_lines\",\n            Stdin: generateLines(1, 2500),\n            ExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n                \"xaa\": generateLines(1, 1000),\n                \"xab\": generateLines(1001, 2000),\n                \"xac\": generateLines(2001, 2500),\n            },\n        },\n        {\n            Name:  \"custom_line_count\",\n            Args:  []string{\"-l\", \"3\"},\n            Stdin: generateLines(1, 7),\n            ExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n                \"xaa\": generateLines(1, 3),\n                \"xab\": generateLines(4, 6),\n                \"xac\": generateLines(7, 7),\n            },\n        },\n        // ... filter tests also use ExpectedFiles\n        {\n            Name:  \"filter_basic\",\n            Args:  []string{\"-l\", \"3\", \"--filter=cat > $FILE\"},\n            Stdin: generateLines(1, 5),\n            ExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n                \"xaa\": generateLines(1, 3),\n                \"xab\": generateLines(4, 5),\n            },\n        },\n    }\n}\n```\n\nBoth the Go and GNU binaries run with identical args/stdin/workdir, then all listed files are compared.\n\n**File location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5449/cmd/split/split_test.go` (375 lines)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Full testutils/difftest.go Content\n\n**File location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5449/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (240 lines)\n\nThe core testing harness implementing differential testing:\n\n- **RunDiffTests()**: Runs each test as a subtest, executing both binaries identically\n- **runBinary()**: Executes binary with context timeout (10 seconds), captures stdout/stderr/exit code\n- **applyNormalizers()**: Applies transformation functions to both binaries' outputs before comparison\n- **compareOutputs()**: Checks stdout, stderr, and exit code match\n- **checkExpectedFiles()**: Validates files created match expected content\n- **buildEnv()**: Merges test env with process env, sets LC_ALL=C as default\n- **NormalizeFunc**: Type alias for `func([]byte) []byte` for output transformation\n- **TimestampNormalizer**: Built-in normalizer replacing common timestamp patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n- **ComposeNormalizers()**: Combines multiple normalizers into one\n\n**Environment handling**: Test env KEY=VALUE pairs override process env, LC_ALL=C is always set to normalize locale-dependent output.\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways for Implementing a New Utility\n\n1. **main() structure**: SIGPIPE handler → parse args → open files → process → flush → exit\n2. **Error format**: `\"{command}: {error}\\n\"` to stderr, set exit code before os.Exit()\n3. **Flag parsing**: Custom parser supporting both short and long forms, validation before processing\n4. **Testing**: Use DiffTest with differential testing against GNU tools, normalize outputs for comparison\n5. **File tests**: Use ExpectedFiles map for commands that produce output files\n6. **Normalizers**: Define regex replacements for binary-name, error format, timestamp variations"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45d3aba9-7d8f-4e0d-9de7-7f8799bb40c2","uuid":"0882c379-6b8d-42f6-9be9-7f2122cec234","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:48:09.716Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand patterns used in this Go codebase for implementing a new cmd/ utility. Find and show me:\n\n1. An example of a simple cmd/ ut